│  togi   22:14:00   tuning 0h00m   session 0h00m   0 failures · 0 crashes
│
│  ► NIGHT since 22:13 · 0h30m  ───  mapping CCD 1 at -20  ───  9:20 left
│
│  │             the current trial.
│  │
│  │ RULES       How togi decides what to do: https://github.com/shgew/togi/blob/main/docs/spec/tuner.md
│  │
│  │
│  │ WORDS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│  │
│  │ offset        Curve Optimizer counts, 0 to -50; deeper is more negative
│  │ trial         one launch of one workload on its target
│  │ D             the tuning unit's applied day offset; saved and proposed profiles are not hardware readback
│  │ C             the hard night ceiling, with its edge and margin witnesses; unknown U blocks ordinary promotion
│  │ S             non-authorizing statistical diagnostic, with its slope, witnesses and gaps; never permission or a retreat trigger
│  │ U             the night edge: the shallowest offset that failed in isolation; unknown until mapped, censored when nothing failed down to the limit
│  │ slope         how fast a class's failure rate grows with depth: a fallback until enough is measured
│  │ bound by      what limits diagnostic S: a class's failure rate, edge margin, or baseline; not what permits D
│  │ covered       a class with diagnostic exposure; this does not qualify a whole profile
│  │ hold          clean observed hours at the current exact D; earlier profiles, nights and paused time do not count
│  │ step          hold, promote one tuning unit, retreat, restore, or reset after a firmware change
│  │ veto          a profile an event forbids until the veto clears
│  │ freeze        keeps D and blocks promotions; a required retreat or firmware reset still applies
│  │ qualifying    running a whole profile until every class has witnessed it
│  │ reproducing   re-running a daily event's conditions to see whether it comes back
│  █ share         the part of the night's elapsed time a queue has used, against the part it is meant to take
│  █ allowance     machine-wide consumed and remaining events, including provisional charges; reclassification does not refund them and finish does not hide
│  █               later events
│  █ experimental  experimental: 50 clean hours; at most 1 crash per 17 h (95%, fixed-rate model). This is an example for current exact-profile evidence, not
│  █               a reliability certificate; finish alone never meets the hazard goal
│  █
│  █
│  █ KINDS OF LOAD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│  █
│  █ R1 light          one light thread: compiling, browsing
│  █ R2 heavy vector   one AVX2/AVX-512 thread: encoding, rendering
│  █ R3 load steps     load switching on and off: current steps
│  █ R4 partial load   light load at 25-75% duty: bursty work
│  █ R5 both threads   both threads of one core: SMT pressure
│  █ R6 idle + bursts  idle with short wake-ups: idle and boost
│  █ R7 all-core       a CCD, part of one, or every core: power and heat
│
